               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>ASPARAGUS</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>ASPARAGUS</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Asparagus are one of the most nutritionally  balanced plant-bas</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Asparagus are one of the most nutritionally  balanced plant-based foods. Their great versatility allows them to be eaten  in many ways.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>SautÃ©ed or blanched, lightly  seasoned, they are perfect as a  </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>SautÃ©ed or blanched, lightly  seasoned, they are perfect as a  side dish.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Keep them refrigerated, between 34Â°F and 40Â°F.  Choose asparagu</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Keep them refrigerated, between 34Â°F and 40Â°F.  Choose asparagus with  firm consistency.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>ORGANIC GRAPE TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>ORGANIC GRAPE TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Organic grape tomato is a sweet, bite-sized tomato. Ideal size </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Organic grape tomato is a sweet, bite-sized tomato. Ideal size for many recipes, inluding salads and snacks. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>As snack because of their size,  theyâ€™re ideal to eat in oner b</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>As snack because of their size,  theyâ€™re ideal to eat in oner bite.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName> ORGANIC ROMA  TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText> ORGANIC ROMA  TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Roma tomato is a very traditional variety,  with a firm consist</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Roma tomato is a very traditional variety,  with a firm consistency, mild flavor,  and an ideal size for many recipes. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>A basic ingredient when creating sauces wheter for pasta or hot</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>A basic ingredient when creating sauces wheter for pasta or hot sauces.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>ORGANIC TOMATOES ON THE VINE</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>ORGANIC TOMATOES ON THE VINE</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Organic tomato on the vine remains in its original bunches and </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Organic tomato on the vine remains in its original bunches and continue to ripen even in the kitchen,  maintaining their freshness and flavor. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Ideal for stuffing and salads. Cut in slices for sandwiches, bu</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Ideal for stuffing and salads. Cut in slices for sandwiches, burgers  and pizzas.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>ORGANIC CHERRY TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>ORGANIC CHERRY TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Among all the varieties of tomatoes,  this is a small round tom</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Among all the varieties of tomatoes,  this is a small round tomato, with a sweet flavor.  Ideal for salads and snacks. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Ideal for snacks and salads. Can be cooked in pastas, stews and</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Ideal for snacks and salads. Can be cooked in pastas, stews and stir-fries.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Keep them at an ideal temperature, between 50Â°F and 55.4Â°F.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>ORGANIC MEDLEY TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>ORGANIC MEDLEY TOMATOES</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Full of juicy flavor that will burst with every bite.  This var</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Full of juicy flavor that will burst with every bite.  This variety of tomato is small and round,  ideal as a snack or for salads. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
